\pard\plain \s3\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\cgrid 
Detailed Description\par
\pard\plain 
{
\pard\plain \s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid {\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
Main unit test runner to verify all MC/DC requirements based on .gcov coverage output from the two 'testsuite' programs. \par
}{\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
This file contains test functions necessary to verify each of the GCC MCDC tool requirements. It reads .gov output files generated from running two mcdc test programs, 'gcc_testsuite_gcov_19.c' and '{\field {\*\fldinst { HYPERLINK  \\l "AAAAAAAAAA" }{}}{\fldrslt {\cs37\ul\cf2 additional_gcc_testsuite.c}}}', with coverage turned on, into a database providing queries. The gcov output is inspected by querying the database, comparing to expected coverage reporting. This testrunner uses the "Mini_UT-Assert' unit test framework from {\field {\*\fldinst { HYPERLINK "https://github.com/lore-prokop/Mini_UT-Assert" }{}}{\fldrslt {\cs37\ul\cf2 https://github.com/lore-prokop/Mini_UT-Assert}}}
, a smaller version of the NASA Open Source lightweight framework originally from {\field {\*\fldinst { HYPERLINK "https://sourceforge.net/projects/cfs-ut-assert/files/" }{}}{\fldrslt {\cs37\ul\cf2 https://sourceforge.net/projects/cfs-ut-assert/files/}}}
. \par
 A paper describing this work can be found at //https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/11732044. \par
 \par
{{\s5\sb90\sa30\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs16\cgrid 
Author\par}\pard\plain \s81\li360\widctlpar\ql\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {\s17 \sa60 \sb30
Lorraine Prokop \par
}}{{\s5\sb90\sa30\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs16\cgrid 
Copyright\par}\pard\plain \s81\li360\widctlpar\ql\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {\s17 \sa60 \sb30
GNU Public License {
\par
\pard\plain \s41\li360\widctlpar\adjustright \shading1000\cbpat8 \f2\fs16\cgrid **  Usage:\par
**             gcc -DUT_VERBOSE [-DUT_VERBOSE_TEST_NAME for each test name]\par
**             * Must compile and link with utassert .h and .o files:\par
**                - utassert, utlist, uttest, uttools [.h, .c]\par
**             * Must also have generated two .gcov files for input, one \par
**               from 'gcc_testsuite_gcov-19.c", available as 'gov-19.c' from\par
**               [gcc.git] / gcc / testsuite / gcc.misc-tests / gcov-19.c; and\par
**               the other from 'additional_gcc_testsuite.c' within this distro\par
**             * See makefile 'makefile-utassert-ver-tests' for details\par
**  Global_reads_writes:\par
**             There are two global variables used throughout this file, 'db'\par
**             and 'db_add'.  'db' holds the contents of the .gcov file \par
**             generated by gcc_testsuite_gcov_19, and 'db_add' holds the \par
**             .gcov output from additional_gcc_testsuite\par
**  Overall Algorithm:\par
**     Read each .gcov input file into a dynamically allocated database\par
**     For each requirement in the MCDC Tool Operational Requirements (TOR)\par
**       Interpret the one or both of the .gcov files' data for correctness\par
**         Query the database for statistic of interest\par
**         Compare with expected gcov output\par
**         Pass or Fail the test based on the comparison\par
**\par
**  Expected Output Summary:    Tests Executed:     43\par
**                              Assert Pass Count:  486\par
**                             Assert Fail Count:  0\par
**\par
**  Limitations,Assumptions,Notes:\par
**  Assumes availability of utassert unit test framework\par
**     Assumes .gcov files were previously created corresponding to each\par
**       of the two testsuites\par
**     The database functions were primarily co-pilot generated, the main\par
**       program and tests were hand coded to assure expected values were\par
**       correct\par
**  File History:\par
**   MM/DD/YYYY  Author                DESCRIPTION\par
**   ----------  --------------------- ----------------------------------------\par
**   03/24/2026  Lorraine Prokop       Initial version & doc complete\par
**               lore.prokop@gmail.com \par
**   10/20/2026  Lorraine Prokop        github Issue 1 changes to better support\par
**                                     multiple gcc versons -- block numbering\par
**                                     changes between versions, so keying on \par
**                                     source file line number instead. Changed\par
**                                     over 300 tests...\par
** }
 \par
}}}}
