Pointer to the newly created BranchInfo record\par
}}Ensures sufficient capacity for a new BranchInfo entry by growing the branch array when full Initializes the new record to zero, assigns the branch and block identifiers, allocates the initial condition array, and returns a pointer to the new entry {
\par
\pard\plain \s41\li360\widctlpar\adjustright \shading1000\cbpat8 \f2\fs16\cgrid ** Global_reads_writes Reads: f->num_branches  f->cap_branches\par
**         f->branches  Writes: f->num_branches  f->cap_branches  f->branches\par
**         and fields of the new record\par
** Limitations,Assumptions,Notes\par
**          - Caller must provide a valid FunctionInfo pointer\par
**          - Capacity grows by doubling when full\par
**          - Function terminates the program on allocation failure\par
** Algorithm:\par
**   If the branch array is full:\par
**       Double the capacity\par
**       Reallocate the branch array to the new size\par
**       If reallocation fails:\par
**           Print an error and exit\par
**   Select the next free BranchInfo slot and increment the count\par
**   Clear the new record with memset\par
**   Store the branch_id and line_num\par
**   Allocate the initial condition array with capacity 4\par
**   If allocation fails:\par
**       Print an error and exit\par
**   Return a pointer to the new BranchInfo record\par
** History\par
**   03/24/2026  Lore/Copilot  Initial documentation added\par
**   10/20/2026  Lore Prokop   Per git issue #1, changed to Line Number Keying\par
**                             rather than block id keying\par
** }
 \par
}}
