Reads the .gcov file line by line, identifies function boundaries, counts source lines, blocks, branches, calls, and condition coverage, and updates the corresponding structures in the database The parser relies on gcov's textual output format and extracts numeric identifiers and coverage counts using sscanf and string matching {
\par
\pard\plain \s41\li360\widctlpar\adjustright \shading1000\cbpat8 \f2\fs16\cgrid ** Global_reads_writes Reads: file contents  Writes: db->funcs and all\par
**         nested coverage fields\par
** Limitations,Assumptions,Notes\par
**          - Caller must provide valid filename and db pointers\par
**          - Function terminates the program on file open failure\par
**          - Parsing depends on gcov's output format and may break if the\par
**            format changes\par
**          - Only the patterns used by this project are recognized\par
** Algorithm:\par
**   Open the .gcov file for reading\par
**   If the file cannot be opened:\par
**       Print an error and exit\par
**   Initialize state: no current function and last_block_id = -1\par
**   For each line in the file:\par
**       Trim whitespace\par
**       Skip empty lines\par
**       If inside a function:\par
**           Detect numbered source lines and count unique line numbers\par
**       If the line begins with "function":\par
**           Extract the function name\par
**           Retrieve or create the FunctionInfo record\par
**           Reset line and block tracking fields\par
**           Continue to next line\par
**       If no current function:\par
**           Continue to next line\par
**       Detect "call 0" lines and count calls not taken\par
**       Detect block lines containing "-block <n>":\par
**           Increment total block count\par
**           If execution count is "%%%%%:":\par
**               Increment blocks_not_taken\par
**       Detect uncovered lines marked "#####:"\par
**           Increment uncovered line count\par
**       Detect block identifier lines and update last_block_id\par
**       Detect condition coverage lines "condition outcomes covered N/M":\par
**           Update branch condition coverage and function totals\par
**       Detect branch lines:\par
**           Add a new branch record\par
**           Record taken count and update branches_taken_zero if needed\par
**       Detect condition not covered lines:\par
**           Add a new condition record and mark missing outcomes\par
**   Close the file\par
** History\par
**   03/24/2026  Lore/Copilot  Initial code complete & documentation added\par
** }
 \par
}}
