\pard \widctlpar\intbl\adjustright
{in,out\cell }{{\i s} \cell }{Pointer to a null-terminated character buffer to be trimmed The buffer contents are modified in place and must not be NULL\cell }
{\row }
}
Performs two trimming operations: 1) Leading trim: advances a pointer past leading spaces or tabs and shifts the remaining characters left using memmove() 2) Trailing trim: walks backward from the end of the string and replaces trailing whitespace with '\\0' {
\par
\pard\plain \s41\li360\widctlpar\adjustright \shading1000\cbpat8 \f2\fs16\cgrid ** Global_reads_writes Reads: none  Writes: none (operates only on the\par
**         caller-provided buffer)** Limitations,Assumptions,Notes:\par
**          - Caller must provide a writable, null-terminated buffer\par
**          - Behavior undefined if s is NULL\par
**          - Only ASCII whitespace is trimmed\par
**          - memmove() is used to safely handle overlapping regions\par
** Algorithm:\par
**   p = s\par
**   Set p to the start of the string\par
**   Advance p while it points to a leading space or tab\par
**   If p moved forward:\par
**       Shift the remaining characters left using memmove()\par
**   Compute the current length of the string\par
**   While the last character is whitespace:\par
**       Replace it with '\\0' and reduce the length\par
**   Stop when no trailing whitespace remains\par
** History:\par
**   03/24/2026  Lore/Copilot  Initial documentation added\par
** }
 \par
}}
